<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yashaskara</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">reigned 939–948</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Yashaskara was a king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kashmir">Kashmir</a>, chosen by an assembly of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brahmins">Brahmins</a> in 939 after years of strife among the palace guards and court factions that had followed the Utpala dynasty's decline. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajatarangini">Kalhana's Rajatarangini</a> presents him as a just ruler who restored order. After his death in 948 power soon passed to the minister <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/parvagupta">Parvagupta</a>, founder of a new dynasty.</p></div>
